<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>{{ post.title }} | HVTracker</title>
  <meta name="description" content="{{ post.excerpt }}">
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://hvtracker.net/blog/{{ post.slug }}/">
  <meta property="og:type" content="article">
  <meta property="og:title" content="{{ post.title }}">
  <meta property="og:description" content="{{ post.excerpt }}">
  <meta property="og:url" content="https://hvtracker.net/blog/{{ post.slug }}/">
  <meta property="og:image" content="https://hvtracker.net/og-v2.png">
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
  <meta name="twitter:title" content="{{ post.title }}">
  <meta name="twitter:description" content="{{ post.excerpt }}">
  <meta name="twitter:image" content="https://hvtracker.net/og-v2.png">
  <script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Article",
    "headline": {{ post.title | tojson }},
    "description": {{ post.excerpt | tojson }},
    "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "HVTracker", "url": "https://hvtracker.net" },
    "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "HVTracker", "url": "https://hvtracker.net" },
    "datePublished": "{{ post.date_iso }}",
    "dateModified": "{{ post.date_iso }}",
    "mainEntityOfPage": "https://hvtracker.net/blog/{{ post.slug }}/"
  }
  </script>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/site.css?v={{ css_hash }}">
  <style>
    *,*::before,*::after{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}
    :root{--muted:#6f665d}
    body{background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font:17px/1.7 var(--font-sans)}
    a{color:inherit}
    .page{max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;padding:24px 24px 56px}
    .logo{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-weight:700;font-size:20px;text-decoration:none}.logo span{color:var(--lobster)}
    .crumb{font:12px var(--font-mono);color:var(--muted);margin:18px 0 26px}
    h1{font-size:32px;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.02em;margin-bottom:10px}
    .meta{font:13px var(--font-mono);color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:26px}
    h2{font-size:21px;margin:34px 0 12px}
    p{margin:0 0 16px}
    table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px;margin:0 0 10px}
    th{font:11px var(--font-mono);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--muted);text-align:left;padding:6px 10px 6px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
    td{padding:7px 10px 7px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
    td.num{font-family:var(--font-mono)}
    .note{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)}
    .foot{margin-top:38px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)}
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">
  <a class="logo" href="/">HV<span>Tracker</span></a>
  <div class="crumb"><a href="/blog/">Blog</a> / State of Agent Trust</div>
  <article>
    <h1>{{ post.title }}</h1>
    <div class="meta">{{ post.date_display }} · {{ post.stats.start_date }} → {{ post.stats.end_date }} · {{ post.stats.snapshot_days }} daily snapshots · CC BY 4.0</div>

    <p>{{ post.excerpt }}</p>
    <p class="note">Every figure below is computed from HVTracker's public daily registry snapshots for the quarter — the same data anyone can download and recheck. Methodology version{{ "s" if post.stats.methodology_versions|length != 1 else "" }} active during the quarter: {{ post.stats.methodology_versions | join(", ") }}. Because scoring definitions can change between versions, this report tracks <strong>score-independent</strong> ecosystem facts; the grade table is a point-in-time distribution at quarter end, not a trend.</p>
    {% if post.stats.tracking_began %}
    <p class="note"><strong>Coverage note:</strong> HVTracker began daily tracking on {{ post.stats.tracking_began }}, so registry growth this quarter largely reflects the initial roster build-out rather than newly created projects.</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if post.stats.field_baselines %}
    <p class="note"><strong>Signal-capture note:</strong> some signals started being captured during the quarter; their "start" columns baseline at first capture rather than the quarter start — {% for label, d in post.stats.field_baselines.items() %}{{ label }} from {{ d }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</p>
    {% endif %}

    <h2>Registry</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Start of quarter</th><th>End of quarter</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Agents tracked</td><td class="num">{{ post.stats.agents_start }}</td><td class="num">{{ post.stats.agents_end }}</td></tr>
        <tr><td>MCP servers implemented</td><td class="num">{{ post.stats.mcp_start }}</td><td class="num">{{ post.stats.mcp_end }}</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Build provenance published</td><td class="num">{{ post.stats.provenance_start }}</td><td class="num">{{ post.stats.provenance_end }}</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Stale (no push ≥ 90 days)</td><td class="num">{{ post.stats.stale_start }}</td><td class="num">{{ post.stats.stale_end }}</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>{{ post.stats.newly_listed }} project{{ "s" if post.stats.newly_listed != 1 else "" }} entered the registry during the quarter; {{ post.stats.delisted }} left active tracking.</p>

    <h2>Provider dependencies at quarter end</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Agents depending on it</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for p in post.stats.top_providers %}
        <tr><td>{{ p.name }}</td><td class="num">{{ p.count }}</td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    {% if post.stats.provider_gainers %}
    <p>Fastest-growing dependencies this quarter: {% for g in post.stats.provider_gainers %}{{ g.name }} (+{{ g.delta }}){% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</p>
    {% endif %}

    <h2>Trust-grade distribution at quarter end</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Grade</th><th>A</th><th>B</th><th>C</th><th>D</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Agents</td><td class="num">{{ post.stats.grades_end.A }}</td><td class="num">{{ post.stats.grades_end.B }}</td><td class="num">{{ post.stats.grades_end.C }}</td><td class="num">{{ post.stats.grades_end.D }}</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="foot">
      Auto-generated from registry snapshots at render time — no numbers are written by hand. Data: CC BY 4.0, attribution "HVTracker (hvtracker.net)". Live charts: <a href="/trends/">/trends/</a> · Method: <a href="/methodology/">/methodology/</a> · Verify any score: <a href="/methodology/#verify-yourself">verify yourself</a>.
    </div>
  </article>
</div>
</body>
</html>
